WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.330
As one of the young breakthrough stars of
the Harry Potter film franchise, Tom Felton

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:08.290
grew up in front of the whole world, right
alongside his character, the villainous Draco

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.290
Malfoy.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:13.349
He may not have been a member of the heroic
trinity in the series, but among Potter fans,

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:15.920
Felton's name became just about as well-known
as his co-stars.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.849
So, it seemed logical that he'd be among those
who'd slither in to the A-list after the series

00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:23.310
came to an end in 2011.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.069
Unlike some of the others, though, Felton
has since struggled to shed his status as

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:31.069
an alumnus of Hogwarts, which means his career
outside of the World of Witchcraft and Wizardry

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:33.120
has been anything but magical.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.440
Whereas Daniel Radcliffe has become something
of an indie sensation and Emma Watson headlined

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.100
an entirely different blockbuster with curses
and castles, Tom Felton hasn't been able to

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.469
ride his Nimbus 2000 to the top of the Hollywood
ladder just yet.

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:49.460
Let's take a look at some of the reasons Hollywood
won't cast him anymore.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.789
Conflicted feelings

00:00:50.789 --> 00:00:55.530
Starring in an eight-film mega-movie franchise
might seem like the opportunity of a lifetime

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.880
for any actor, but Tom Felton didn't cherish
the experience of being an overnight cinematic

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.110
success story as much as others might.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:06.410
Before the final film Deathly Hallows, Part
2 hit theaters, he told the Daily Mail that

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.890
he looked forward to the "freedom" of not
starring in the films anymore, saying:

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:13.119
"One thing that people keep on saying to me
is that the wealth and the fame must have

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:15.270
made up for missing out on my childhood.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.240
But the idea of money, putting a price on
your childhood, is ridiculous.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.100
To me, fame is not a positive thing.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.280
The idea of being famous is a lot better than
the reality.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.860
It's fantastic when you go to premieres and
people cheer you, but it's not real."

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:31.290
Considering most of those fans who were cheering
him on at those very premieres were the ones

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.140
he'd need to see his next movies, those words
may have come back to bite him harder than

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.140
Nagini.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.020
A career left turn

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:42.090
After Harry Potter, Daniel Radcliffe decided
to give the Broadway circuit and small-budget

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.090
films a whirl.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:46.830
And Emma Watson went to college, became a
beauty brand ambassador, and left Hermione

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.950
behind with films like The Bling Ring and
This Is the End.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.219
"I'm not f---ing around!"

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:54.920
Meanwhile, Tom Felton's first big post-Potter
move was to rap.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.180
Yes, rap.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.369
In 2011, Felton revealed that he'd scored
a recording deal with an independent label

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:02.100
to produce some hip-hop music, saying:

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.710
"I was thinking of doing some N-Dubz-style
stuff.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.909
I am looking to get into the grime rap UK
scene."

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:11.820
Felton added that he intended to "change [his]
image," and although that public persona overhaul

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:15.530
never seemed to pan out, some of his music
has made way to the public sphere.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.291
However, despite a few EP releases and a moderate
amount of viral attention on YouTube, his

00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:24.420
music has hardly been successful enough to
qualify as a new career path.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:25.420
Too familiar

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.380
His emcee effort might've at least been a
change of pace, but Felton's next big screen

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:32.780
adventure was far too similar to his Harry
Potter persona.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.560
Felton claims he's not at all like the kid
that made him famous…

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:40.650
"To be honest, I'm very un-Malfoy like in
my day-to-day biddings"

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:46.250
However, in 2011's Rise of the Planet of the
Apes, he played a small part as Dodge Landon,

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:51.240
a cruel zoo security guard who tortures the
film's central sentient ape, Caesar.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:56.200
"Take your stinking paw off me you damn dirty
ape."

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.430
Like Draco, the character is remarkable only
for his sniveling demeanor and the ease with

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.620
which audiences root against him.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.260
Between this role and his villainous TV turn
on TNT's Murder In the First, he may not be

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.090
distancing himself from the role that made
him famous, which could make him seem a little

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.000
one-note to casting directors.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.100
Indeed, even Radcliffe has had to work hard
to extricate himself from the world of broomsticks

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.870
and floo powder, taking roles that are far
off the mark of the Boy Who Lived.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:25.630
By heading right back into an unlikable mini-baddie
role after Deathly Hallows, Felton may have

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.360
made a huge career misstep right from the
start.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.060
Regaining confidence

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:33.980
Another surprising downside to the safety
of a long-lived role like Felton had in the

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.910
Harry Potter series is that the series' end
can feel a little like being thrown into the

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.570
ocean without a life vest.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:43.230
The actor has admitted that returning to the
regular practice of auditioning for parts

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:47.360
to sustain a lifestyle, rather than just trying
to fill in the blanks between sequels, was

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.730
very difficult for him to adjust to.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.810
He told the Daily Mail in 2011:

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.870
"I'm much more nervous in auditions now than
I was at 11.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.120
You take a lot of hits before you get something
good.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.620
The first few were heartbreaking."

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.760
The disappointment of being denied certain
roles was so disorienting for him, in fact,

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.340
that he considered walking away from the business
altogether, saying:

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.280
"I thought, 'I can't do this.'

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.210
They are cutthroat in America.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.570
Before you've even started, someone's playing
on the BlackBerry.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:15.140
You're reading your lines, physically convulsing,
and they just say 'Thank you.'

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.650
That means, 'Get lost.'

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.269
I did 19 auditions and got the 20th, for the
film The Apparition."

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:25.270
To make matters worse, that movie would mark
the start of a series of box office flops.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.639
Missing box office magic

00:04:26.639 --> 00:04:31.120
Although the Harry Potter series was a box
office phenomenon, Felton has still not proven

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.160
himself to be a bankable actor.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:37.610
His small-time thriller pic The Apparition
failed to recoup its financiers' investment,

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:42.719
despite having both a Harry Potter star and
Twilight alum Ashley Greene leading the cast.

00:04:42.719 --> 00:04:46.379
Since then, he's yet to appear in a film that
made any kind of impression at the ticket

00:04:46.379 --> 00:04:47.379
booth.

00:04:47.379 --> 00:04:51.469
Even movies that have been relatively well-received
by critics, like the regal biopic Belle and

00:04:51.469 --> 00:04:55.930
A United Kingdom, featured him only in supporting
roles and brought in very little money during

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.990
their small theatrical runs.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:01.379
Felton's not the only one of the Harry Potter
alums who has struggled to convince muggles

00:05:01.379 --> 00:05:05.720
to see his movies, but being associated with
so many bombs likely isn't making his new

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.900
agent's job any easier.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:09.009
Blond ambition

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:13.060
Considering his dismal box office streak,
Tom Felton's chances of nabbing a leading

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.639
movie role anytime soon seem low, but it might
not be a good idea to tell him that.

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:22.289
In fact, the actor's ambitions seem to be
unfettered, he not only wants another franchise,

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:27.980
but he wants one of the most iconic and long-lasting
of all time: Bond, James Bond.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:33.250
He told Metro that playing the suave 007 agent
is an "unfulfilled career ambition" for him,

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.250
adding:

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.530
"I haven't landed James Bond yet.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:39.360
Playing Bond or a Bond villain was why I wanted
to do movies in the first place."

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.949
Considering that may be the most coveted role
in all of Hollywood, his expectations may

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:46.660
be a bit lofty and unrealistic.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.280
Time to turn it around

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:53.729
These days, Tom Felton does seem to be settling
in with a more low-key professional lifestyle.

00:05:53.729 --> 00:05:59.289
In 2016, for example, he nabbed a recurring
role in the third season of The CW's The Flash,

00:05:59.289 --> 00:06:02.939
and while the role didn't carry on to the
next season, it did help introduce him to

00:06:02.939 --> 00:06:05.889
a new and different fanbase in the comics
community.

00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:10.560
He was also cast in the little-seen, but ambitious
adaptation of William Shakespeare's Hamlet,

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:15.060
titled Ophelia, alongside some big names like
Daisy Ridley and Naomi Watts.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.659
Neither project has put him on a new trajectory
for success yet, but they have helped Felton

00:06:19.659 --> 00:06:23.930
stretch into new territory that might better
convince casting agents he's capable of doing

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:27.050
more than a bunch of Draco Malfoy impressions
in the future.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.050
Thanks for watching!

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:30.259
